---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Route planner privacy and service terms">
  <a href="/route-planner/">← Route planner</a>
  <h1>Route planner privacy and service terms</h1>
  <h2>Your journey data</h2>
  <p>Opening the planner loads OpenStreetMap tiles. The tile service receives your IP address and the displayed map area. “Use my location” asks your browser for permission and fills the starting point.</p>
  <p>Submitting the form sends your trip to the backend, OpenAI and the route services: FOSSGIS for walking, transport.opendata.ch for Swiss transit and address lookup, and Overpass/OpenStreetMap for restaurants. The private adapter uses osm-api-js only to read map objects.</p>
  <p>Your OpenAI key authenticates three tool decisions and a final explanation. It is cleared after submission and never stored by this app or forwarded to map services or MCP.</p>
  <p>Trip sessions expire after three minutes. Bounded in-memory caches retain transit responses for 30 seconds, walking paths and location lookups for 24 hours, nearby restaurants for five minutes and OSM tags for one hour. Restarting the service clears them. No journey history is saved in the database.</p>
  <h2>Service terms</h2>
  <p>Map data is © <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap contributors</a>. Public <a href="https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/tiles/">tile services</a> and <a href="https://routing.openstreetmap.de/about.html">FOSSGIS routing</a> have usage limits; this preview caches requests and limits provider calls to one per second. Swiss timetables come from <a href="https://transport.opendata.ch/docs.html">transport.opendata.ch</a>. AI processing follows <a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy/">OpenAI’s privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <p>Solid lines follow walking paths. Dashed transit lines connect published stops, not exact tracks. Transit distance is unavailable; its displayed distance covers walking only. Opening hours do not confirm kitchen service, dishes or prices. Restaurants with uncertain hours are omitted. Check disruptions and restaurant sources before travelling.</p>
</BaseLayout>
<style>h1{margin:1.5rem 0;font-size:2rem}h2{margin:2rem 0 1rem}p{max-width:750px;line-height:1.8}p a{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}</style>
